/*! @brief HttpServer is one of the built-in objects, it is an object used to create HTTP servers. An HttpServer object contains two required parameters: port and event handler interface object. In the event handler interface object, the specific implementation can be a simple callback function, or complex routing, chain processing arrays, etc.

The http server object is a combination and encapsulation of TcpServer and HttpHandler, convenient for quickly building servers, logically equivalent to:
```JavaScript
var svr = new net.TcpServer(addr, port, new http.Handler(function(req){
   ...
}));
```

Below is the simplest application example of HttpServer, it just returns the string hello world for all requests.
```JavaScript
const http = require('http');
var svr = new http.Server(8080, (req) => {
    req.response.write('hello, world');
});
svr.start();
```

From the code, we can see that first, we imported the built-in http module. Then we created a new HttpServer object and passed in two necessary parameters: one is the port number, the other is the specific event handler interface object. In this example, we used a simple callback function as the event handler interface to respond to data from HTTP requests. Where `req.response.write('hello, world')` is used to respond our string hello world to the client.

After completing the creation of the HttpServer object, use `svr.start()` to start the server, so that we can receive HTTP requests from the Internet through this server.
 */
interface HttpServer : TcpServer
{
    /*! @brief HttpServer constructor, listen on all local addresses
    @param port specifies the http server listening port
    @param hdlr http built-in message processor, processing function, chain processing array, routing object, see mq.Handler for details
   */
    HttpServer(Integer port, Handler hdlr);

    /*! @brief HttpServer constructor
    @param addr specifies the http server listening address, "" means listen on all local addresses
    @param port specifies the http server listening port
    @param hdlr http built-in message processor, processing function, chain processing array, routing object, see mq.Handler for details
   */
    HttpServer(String addr, Integer port, Handler hdlr);

    /*! @brief HttpServer constructor
    @param addr specifies the http server listening address, "" means listen on all local addresses
    @param hdlr http built-in message processor, processing function, chain processing array, routing object, see mq.Handler for details
   */
    HttpServer(String addr, Handler hdlr);

    /*! @brief Allow cross-origin requests
     @param allowHeaders specifies accepted http header fields
     */
    enableCrossOrigin(String allowHeaders = "Content-Type");

    /*! @brief Query and set the maximum number of request headers, default is 128 */
    Integer maxHeadersCount;

    /*! @brief Query and set the maximum request header length, default is 8192 */
    Integer maxHeaderSize;

    /*! @brief Query and set the maximum body size in MB, default is 64 */
    Integer maxBodySize;

    /*! @brief Automatic decompression function switch, default off */
    Boolean enableEncoding;

    /*! @brief Query and set the server name, default is: fibjs/0.x.0 */
    String serverName;
};